  {
   "unit_id": "unit-8f67f07080b0482fb3929e22fc41b6e5",
   "title": "Heartbeat leak rediscovery",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The assistant re‑examines heap retainer paths and discovers two compounding bugs in the heartbeat helper: each closed socket carries an array of ~61 'pong' listeners and the repeating Timeout is never cleared.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c2-t034",
       "char_start": 75,
       "char_end": 229
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "This explains why earlier listener counts were flat — the leak was on per‑socket emitters silenced by setMaxListeners(0).",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c2-t036",
       "char_start": 75,
       "char_end": 218
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c2-t031",
    "synth-c2-t032",
    "synth-c2-t033",
    "synth-c2-t034",
    "synth-c2-t035",
    "synth-c2-t036"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
   "frozen": true,
   "created_at_turn": "synth-c2-t049"
  },
  {
   "unit_id": "unit-1f303775c0d846fbbe8ffb92c7161e3a",
   "title": "Heartbeat fix implementation",
   "summary_sentences": [
    {
     "text": "The assistant patches heartbeat.js to register a single pong listener, clear the interval on close, and remove the setMaxListeners(0) hack.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c2-t038",
       "char_start": 38,
       "char_end": 150
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "After the patch, per‑socket listener counts consistently show exactly one pong listener per socket and zero intervals after disconnect.",
     "source_spans": [
      {
       "turn_id": "synth-c2-t043",
       "char_start": 354,
       "char_end": 419
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "covered_turns": [
    "synth-c2-t037",
    "synth-c2-t038",
    "synth-c2-t039",
    "synth-c2-t040",
    "synth-c2-t041",
    "synth-c2-t042",
    "synth-c2-t043"
   ],
   "salient_infos": [],
